  "notes": "USAGE:\n{利下|りさ}げ is a noun often used in news and financial reporting. It can also be used with する: {利下|りさ}げする (to cut interest rates). The word is frequently seen in headlines about central bank policy decisions.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {利下|りさ}げを{行|おこな}う (carry out a rate cut)\n- {大幅|おおはば}な{利下|りさ}げ (significant rate cut)\n- {追加|ついか}{利下|りさ}げ (additional rate cut)\n- {利下|りさ}げ{幅|はば} (size of the rate cut)\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- {利上|りあ}げ is the opposite, meaning an interest rate hike.\n- {金利|きんり} means interest rate.\n- {金融|きんゆう}{緩和|かんわ} means monetary easing, a broader policy that includes rate cuts.",
